From 77920cc491d1e5e75e5df80af8a715ca4666af87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:48:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Baseline validators: two settings owners, Field types and
 Runtime settings

World Foundry's baseline level now has two settings owners at one spot
(docs/plans/2026-10-31-baseline-settings-cleanup.md there): "Field types"
(schema FieldTypes, the first editable owner, one field per touch-settings
example) and "Runtime settings" (schema Settings, the only owner of Runtime
Options, with Show FPS authored editable). All three baseline validators
assumed the old three identical owners, and all three checked a schema
name, BaselineSettings, that the level stopped using on 2026-10-22.

baseline-picker: two candidates and one bracket ("2 objects here") as the
first highlight; the phone's Right keeps that highlight; the short list
holds both owners in actor order.

baseline-settings: a two-owner chooser by title; edits, stale-session,
invalid-draft reconnect, Apply readback and Home cancellation now use
Field types rows 1 (int-number), 7 (float-slider) and 17 (str-plain); the
other owner is checked as a separate catalog instead of a second copy.

baseline-runtime-options: the TV opens Runtime settings (row 2, after Pick
in 3D and Field types) and turns Show FPS off as the first row of the first
section. The idle snapshot reports Field types, so Runtime Options values
are read with the Runtime settings form open, and the clock waits key on
the game being idle (the actual clock still proves each rate). The
cross-owner check becomes field_types_unaffected and the reopen check
reopened_owner_reads_process_globals; two-owner synchronisation of process
globals stays covered by World Foundry's host test, since the level now
has one Runtime Options owner. A scripted two-owner host covers the full
sequence and a failing layout.

